tal Sciences","years":[2013]},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I92403157","name":"University of Science and Technology Beijing","years":[2012]},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I1327237609","name":"Ministry of Education of the People's Republic of China","years":[2011]},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4210140193","name":"Jiangsu Provincial Academy of Environmental Science","years":[2010]},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I881766915","name":"Nanjing University","years":[2009,2010]},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4210090489","name":"State Key Laboratory of Pollution Control and Resource Reuse","years":[2009,2010]},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I200296433","name":"Chinese Academy of Medical Sciences & Peking Union Medical College","years":[2009]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I161318765","name":"University of California, Los Angeles","years":[2004]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I84218800","name":"University of California, Davis","years":[1995]}],"author_id":"A5100599680","ca_plastic_works_count":1,"ca_works_count":1,"citations_by_year":[{"all":907,"plastic":0,"year":2017},{"all":874,"plastic":0,"year":2018},{"all":936,"plastic":0,"year":2019},{"all":1135,"plastic":0,"year":2020},{"all":1234,"plastic":0,"year":2021},{"all":1378,"plastic":0,"year":2022},{"all":1356,"plastic":0,"year":2023},{"all":1454,"plastic":0,"year":2024},{"all":1474,"plastic":0,"year":2025},{"all":1173,"plastic":0,"year":2026}],"cited_by_count":17374,"domain_tags":[],"early_career":false,"first_pub_year":1991,"first_year":2021,"h_index":68,"institution_ids":["I103635307"],"last_year":2021,"m_quotient":1.94,"name":"Xinru Wang","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2636-9546","plastic_basis":"openalex","plastic_citations":0,"plastic_works_count":0,"primary_affiliations":[{"country_code":"CN","id":"I100357981","name":"Wannan Medical College","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I146773158","name":"Qingdao Agricultural University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I179026463","name":"Beijing Technology and Business University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4210092839","name":"Gansu University of Traditional Chinese Medicine","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4210116517","name":"Shandong Provincial Hospital","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4210124809","name":"Peking University People's Hospital","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4210151987","name":"Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4210156501","name":"First Affiliated Hospital of Harbin Medical University","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4210163399","name":"Shandong First Medical University","source":"openalex_last_known"}],"rising_pct":null,"rising_score":null,"work_count":1,"work_ids":["W3121420714"]},"schema_version":"s3.1","works":[{"abstract":"Plasticizers, due to the widespread use of plastics, occur ubiquitously in the environment. The reuse of waste resources (e.g., treated wastewater, biosolids, animal waste) and other practices (e.g., plastic mulching) introduce phthalates into agroecosystems. As a detoxification mechanism, plants are known to convert phthalates to polar monophthalates after uptake, which are followed by further transformations, including conjugation with endogenous biomolecules. The objective of this study was 2-fold: to obtain a complete metabolic picture of the widely used di- n -butyl phthalate (DnBP) by using a suite of complementary techniques, including stable isotope labeling, 14 C tracing, and high-resolution mass spectrometry, and to determine if conjugates are deconjugated in human microsomes to release bioactive metabolites. In Arabidopsis thaliana cells, the primary initial metabolite of DnBP was mono- n -butyl phthalate (MnBP), and MnBP was rapidly metabolized via hydroxylation, carboxylation, glycosylation, and malonylation to seven transformation products. One of the conjugates, MnBP-acyl-\u03b2- d -glucoside (MnBP-Glu), was incubated in human liver (HLM) and intestinal (HIM) microsomes and was found to undergo rapid transformations. Approximately 15% and 10% of MnBP-Glu were deconjugated to the free form MnBP in HIM and HLM, respectively. These findings highlight that phthalates, as diesters, are susceptible to hydrolysis to form monoesters that can be readily conjugated via a phase II metabolism in plants. Conjugates may be deconjugated to release bioactive compounds after human ingestion. Therefore, an accurate assessment of the dietary exposure of phthalates and other contaminants must consider plant metabolites, especially including conjugates, to better predict their potential environmental and human health risks.","author_ids":["A5013564313","A5043005229","A5075951652","A5100599680","A5100688661","A5101979506"],"author_institution_ids":["I103635307"],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":31,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.est.0c07232","domain_tags":["ecotoxicology_and_trophic_transfer","human_exposure_and_health_risk","risk_assessment","soil_and_agriculture","wastewater_and_treatment"],"facet_tags":["matrix:food_and_drink","matrix:soil_and_agriculture","matrix:wastewater"],"institution_ids":["I103635307","I205237279"],"is_oa":false,"journal":"Environmental Science & Technology","last_updated":"2026-11-07T11:25:07.637180","license":"","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"closed","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.est.0c07232","openalex_topics":["T10375","T10419","T10686"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"chemicals-in-plastics","primary_topic":"T10686","pub_date":"2021-01-26","study_type":"article","title":"Conjugation of Di-n-butyl Phthalate Metabolites in Arabidopsis thaliana and Potential Deconjugation in Human Microsomes","type":"article","work_id":"W3121420714","year":2021}]}
